  "id": "COMPOUND:17163 - PROTEIN:5821",
  "verbalization": "Norarecoline is implicated in the biological pathway leading to MOVP-3 through multiple distinct targets within the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family. These targets include compounds such as 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, cholesta-5,7,8(14),22E-tetraen-3-one, and (2R,3S,4S,5R,6S)-2-(Hydroxymethyl)-6-[3-[(E)-3-Hydroxyprop-1-Enyl]-2,5-Dimethoxyphenoxy]Oxane-3,4,5-Triol, all of which are known to interact with MOVP-3. The evidence suggests that Norarecoline may act as a modulator of these SDR family members, potentially influencing MOVP-3 through a shared biochemical mechanism. The final scores from the paths indicate a plausible, though not definitive, relationship, supported by the presence of multiple distinct targets that are all functionally linked to MOVP-3. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition or modulation of enzymes within the SDR family, which could have a broader impact on the metabolic pathways that lead to MOVP-3. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Norarecoline to influence MOVP-3 through a complex, multi-targeted mechanism.",
